  "published_description": "Original computational evidence accompanying Taylor Kalin's technical comment, Equation consistency in electron-only reconnection manuscripts . This software checks displayed equations in arXiv:2407.06020v2, its authentic publisher-hosted CHORUS accepted manuscript dated 19 March 2025, and the supplement embedded in arXiv v2. The subscription version of record and final journal supplement were not obtained. No original GX simulation, raw diagnostic field or numerical reconnection curve is reproduced or rejected. The original exact producer uses rational finite Fourier convolution for 60 periodic energy states, 24 linear-symbol cases, Gaussian/Hermite projection controls and positive reconnection-rate and conditional decay checks. Two explanatory figures are synthetic. Full generalized-flux advection is retained. The original numerical outputs match across Python 3.12.14 and 3.13.7; the plotting runtime uses NumPy 2.3.5 and Matplotlib 3.11.2. Independent review records, original source provenance and separate implementations are preserved. This archive contains all 55 files at computational commit 83583b1524778b8bb4e5c78482ae7f4f104856cc . The byte-verified staged Git tree is 7bf82539dd5224ec9328dc94848b2a62dc6b4029 , a tree identifier distinct from that commit. Manuscript/PDF files, third-party source PDFs, private credentials and original source simulation data are excluded. Archive: electron-only-equation-audit-code-v1.0.0.zip , 393818 bytes; SHA-256 d0444c832c21b8a2e60ebd02e576c4ad2077388dfeb9e412590b7049d1e5aabc ; MD5 ed245136dea9d446645372c7471e3af9 . All members were checked against the public commit. Code is MIT licensed; original documentation and figures are CC BY 4.0. Third-party works retain their rights. Author: Taylor Kalin, ORCID 0009-0003-9000-9315. Self-funded, with AI-assisted checking/programming disclosed. This is a software publication, not manuscript acceptance or independent human peer review. Frozen public source: computational commit on GitHub .",
